# Test Project: Validation of Full Flow

Purpose:
   Minimal project to validate the full SDDRA flow:
   - Prompt → DL2 → decisions → tasks → subtasks
   - SW1 parallel execution with test hierarchy
   - Local Docker test runs
   - CI workflow on PR

Owns: projects/test-project/README.sdd

ProjectStructure:
   - tasks/INDEX.sdd
   - subtasks/INDEX.sdd
   - domains.sdd
   - stack/
   - skills/

ValidationCriteria:
   1. DL2 runs independently: /sdd-decide executes DL2 chain, produces decisions/tasks/subtasks
   2. Handoff to DL1 works: DL1 receives Q/T/ST registry and continues
   3. SW1 executes with test hierarchy: Subtask → Module → System tests run in Docker
   4. Parallel agents: Max 6-10 agents (L0 + 2-4 L1 + 2-4 L2) work concurrently
   5. Local tests pass: All test levels execute in Docker without host tools
   6. CI optimized: PR only runs changed module tests; full suite on merge
   7. Token budget: Coordinator limits context per agent (<8k tokens)
   8. Human gates: 3 gates in DL2 (Q approval, stack approval, plan approval)

Navigation:
   DL2Chain: @../../chains/dl2-decision.sdd
   SW1Chain: @../../chains/swarm.sdd
   TestHierarchy: @../../workflow/test-hierarchy.sdd
   LocalTestExecution: @../../workflow/local-test-execution.sdd
   CIWorkflow: @../../.github/workflows/ci-change-impact.yml

State: +
   (Test project for validating SDDRA flow)
   (Minimal structure to test end-to-end functionality)